{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788929795,"nonce":"/rB0k9GVF4hl/8EmAcdWKypkdtM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABQZOLsQ","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/7","origin":"github"},"title":"Unify AST node tag naming: VarDeclStmt has tag \"VarDecl\"","message":"The interface VarDeclStmt carries the discriminant tag \"VarDecl\", while every other statement node matches tag to interface name (IfStmt/\"IfStmt\", RepeatStmt/\"RepeatStmt\", FuncStmt/\"FuncStmt\", LoopStmt/\"LoopStmt\", ExprStmt/\"ExprStmt\", ReturnStmt/\"ReturnStmt\", Assignment/\"Assignment\"). The expression family is internally consistent the other way: suffix on the interface, dropped on the tag (BinaryExpr/\"Binary\", CallExpr/\"Call\", etc.).\n\nBorn in 992a0fc (first parser commit), before either convention existed; never renamed because the tag is runtime data pinned by the parser and dozens of parser test expectations.\n\nOptions: (a) rename the tag to \"VarDeclStmt\" and update parser + test expectations, or (b) accept the fossil and document the convention in ast.ts.\n\nSurfaced during the semantic-analyzer-diagnostic-harness milestone; deferred per the no-drive-by-fixes rule.","files":null}]}